  <div class="callout"><div class="h">Read this first: ${esc(title)} in four parts</div><p><b>Where the filings are.</b> ${one ? `${esc(lead.name)} County is the whole metro: ${N(lead.filings.ttm.div)} divorce filings at ${N(lead.rates.div_per_1k_married, 1)} per 1,000 married` : `${esc(lead.name)} County carries ${N(lead.filings.ttm.div)} of ${scope} ${N(S.ttm.div)} divorce filings (${P(lead.filings.ttm.div / (S.ttm.div || 1), 0)}) at ${N(lead.rates.div_per_1k_married, 1)} per 1,000 married${hiRate !== lead ? `; the highest rate is ${esc(hiRate.name)} County at ${N(hiRate.rates.div_per_1k_married, 1)}` : ', the highest rate here too'}`}. <b>Where they are growing.</b> ${one ? (isN(lead.rates.div_yoy) && !S.gaps.length ? `${esc(lead.name)} County is ${updown(lead.rates.div_yoy)} on the prior twelve months` : 'No like for like change to report') : growS}${!one ? `; ${codes.length > 1 ? 'the valley' : 'the metro'} as a whole is ${updown((ttG('div') / (S.prev.div || 1) - 1) * 100)}` : ''}. <b>Where the married population is built to divorce.</b> The highest composition hazards among ZIPs with 1,500 or more married adults: ${hiZ.map(z => `${z.zip} ${esc(z.city)} (${N(z.risk.haz_pred, 1)})`).join(', ')}. <b>Where the economy is pushing.</b> ${one ? `${esc(shockC.name)} County's shock index is ${N(shockC.esi, 0)}` : `${esc(shockC.name)} County has ${scope} highest shock index (${N(shockC.esi, 0)})`}; claims run ${isN(cl19) ? N(cl19, 2) + '×' : 'n/a'} the same weeks of 2019 and ${isN(clY) ? N(clY, 2) + '×' : 'n/a'} a year ago${odd ? ' (a swing that large can be a change in how the county\'s claims are counted; check the Texas Workforce Commission series before acting on it)' : ''}, ${N(S.warn12)} workers were on WARN notices in the last twelve months${shrink.length ? `, and payrolls shrank most in ${shrink.map(s => s.name.toLowerCase() + ' (' + sgn(s.chg, 0, '') + ')').join(', ')}` : ''}. ${N(S.exposed)} married adults here live in a household where either spouse is unemployed.</p><p>Court counts exist by county only, so every ZIP filing figure here is an allocation of its county's count (grade C); the Counties view paints the county values themselves. Nothing on this tab describes a household. The filing record, survey precision and the data inventory for the metro are in Ground Truth (module 28).</p></div>
